Package: BayDuBiG
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Durbin-based Bi-level Identification of Spatially Variable Genes
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-09-26
Authors@R: person("Tianyi", "Wang", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "your@email.com")
Description: A Bayesian bi-level variable selection model for identifying
    spatially variable genes (SVGs) in spatial transcriptomics.  The method
    couples a spatial autoregressive (Durbin) term with a two-level spike-and-slab
    prior: a group (pathway) level and a within-group (gene) level.  The group
    effect follows a union semantics (a gene is flagged if at least one of its
    member groups is selected), and false-discovery control is achieved via a
    Bayesian false discovery rate (BFDR) rule.  The MCMC sampler is implemented in
    C++ (RcppArmadillo) with optional OpenMP parallelism.
